name: gozleme bread
components:
  - name: dough
    ingredients:
      - item: full cream greek yogurt
        qty: 0.75
        unit: cup
        note: the fat replaces oil in the dough. non-fat works but comes out tougher
      - item: plain flour
        qty: 1
        unit: cup
        note: no leavening — gozleme is meant to stay flat
      - item: water
        optional: true
        note: by the tsp if the dough won't come together. plain flour is thirstier than SR
      - item: extra virgin olive oil
        qty: 1.5
        unit: tbsp
        note: for frying
      - item: salt
        note: good pinch
      - item: lemon wedges
        note: for serving
    steps:
      - add flour, salt, and yogurt to a large bowl, mixing with a spoon or one hand to form a rough ball. add water a tsp at a time if it stays shaggy
      - transfer to a floured table and knead by hand for 3–5 mins until smooth. sprinkle more flour if too sticky or wet
      - rest covered for 20–30 mins. plain flour builds more gluten than SR, so it springs back when rolled — the long rest is what buys the thinness
  - name: filling
    ingredients:
      - item: spinach
        note: chopped
      - item: feta cheese
      - item: salt
      - item: pepper
    steps:
      - add chopped spinach to a bowl and scrunch with your hands to soften. then crumble in the feta cheese, add salt and pepper, and stir together
  - name: assembly and cook
    steps:
      - cut the dough into 2 equal pieces and roll them into balls
      - dust the table with flour and roll the dough into a thin circle (10–12 inches / 25–30 cm), flipping and sprinkling with flour regularly. roll as thin as possible without tearing
      - add half of the spinach mixture evenly to one half of the dough
      - fold the dough over the filling. press from the fold outward to push the air out before sealing the edges, otherwise you trap a pocket
      - prick the top through with a fork in a few places. the filling steams as it cooks and a sealed parcel has nowhere to vent — this is what balloons it, not the thickness
      - repeat with the 2nd dough
      - heat a large pan over medium heat with 2 teaspoon olive oil. place a gozleme in the pan and cook for 3-5 minutes until golden
      - brush or spray the top with oil, flip it over using a spatula and gently press it to flatten it. keep it pressed as it cooks; prick and flatten any bubble that forms rather than letting it set inflated
      - when golden brown, remove from the pan and place on a board. repeat with the 2nd dough
      - slice into triangles, add a squeeze of lemon and enjoy!
notes: |
  Self raising variant (the old default):
  - Swap the plain flour for 1 cup self raising flour
  - Rest 10 mins instead of 20–30 — softer flour, less springback
  - Puffed up badly even rolled thin. Two causes: the leavening, and steam with
    no vent. Adding 1 tsp baking powder to plain flour to fake SR flour makes it
    worse, so don't
  - The old note "AP flour seems not enough" was never resolved — unclear whether
    it meant not enough flour for the yogurt, or not enough lift. Moot now
  Untested with plain flour as of 2026-08-06 — the liquid may still need adjusting.
